<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <!--
    Lowest-level project: system marker interfaces, architecture attributes, and
    shape interfaces shared by Domain entities and their Application DTOs. Those
    shape interfaces may carry default-implemented members when a rule must have a
    single home across both implementers (IBurnSettingsInfo's early-entry clock) —
    so a little behaviour lives here, deliberately, not just declarations.
    Never a ProjectReference on another Humans.* project — this project stays the
    bottom of the graph so Humans.Domain can reference it. External packages only:
    NodaTime is allowed because IBurnSettingsInfo's calendar members are LocalDate
    and Instant, and NodaTime is an external, base-class-like dependency already
    used by every layer above. Namespaces intentionally remain Humans.Application.*
    (namespace ≠ assembly) so call sites and the Humans.Analyzers full-name
    constants are unaffected by the move.

    G5 lane 3a-1 (nobodies-collective/Humans#866) made this the Base fill: 60 generic files
    arrived from Humans.Application (34), Humans.Domain (16) and Humans.Infrastructure (10) —
    the configuration registry, CacheKeys, the CSV seam, the formatting/timing extensions,
    the cross-cutting cache interfaces and their six IMemoryCache implementations, the
    metering trio, the Serilog enrichers/sink, the GitHub markdown connectors, the role and
    team constants, and four enums. Every one kept its original namespace, so no `using`,
    `_ViewImports`, `<Using Include>` or analyzer full-name constant changed anywhere in the
    repo. The rename of this project to Humans.Base is a later lane. Still zero
    ProjectReference elements — check that before adding one.

    G5 lane 3a-2 followed with the AddSectionDbContext cluster: the generic registration seam
    (SectionDbContextServiceCollectionExtensions), SectionDbContextRegistration,
    SectionMigrationRunner, DatabaseMigrationHostedService, PreMigrationSnapshot,
    SectionMigrationsHistory, QueryMonitoringInterceptor and QueryStatistics. All 28
    table-owning sections call the seam from their own Section.cs and none of them may
    reference Humans.Infrastructure, so Base is the only place it can live. Namespaces
    preserved again (Humans.Infrastructure.Data / .Hosting), so no call site moved.
    InfrastructureServiceCollectionExtensions itself deliberately stayed in
    Humans.Infrastructure — two architecture rules read typeof(…).Assembly off it to mean
    "the Humans.Infrastructure assembly".
  -->

  <!--
    Followed the G5 lane 3a-1 arrivals out of Humans.Application: TrackedCache's
    MarkWarmedForTesting, LoggerTimingExtensions.SelectLogLevel and TrackedLock.WaitToLogLevel
    are internal and were already visible to these two test assemblies from there.
  -->
  <ItemGroup>
    <InternalsVisibleTo Include="Humans.Application.Tests" />
    <InternalsVisibleTo Include="Humans.Users.Tests" />
    <!--
      Followed the G5 lane 3a-2 arrivals: DatabaseMigrationHostedService,
      SectionDbContextRegistration, SectionMigrationRunner and PreMigrationSnapshot are internal
      and stay that way — 26 .Contracts leaves inherit this assembly's public surface, and the
      migration plumbing is not part of it. Humans.Infrastructure still names two of them
      (AddHumansPersistence registers the hosted service, AdminDatabaseDiagnosticsRepository
      injects the registrations) and Humans.Integration.Tests drives SectionMigrationRunner
      directly; both were already inside Humans.Infrastructure's own InternalsVisibleTo set
      before the move.
    -->
    <InternalsVisibleTo Include="Humans.Infrastructure" />
    <InternalsVisibleTo Include="Humans.Integration.Tests" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <PackageReference Include="NodaTime" />
    <!--
      ISection names IServiceCollection and IConfiguration. Both live in the
      shared framework, so this keeps the no-NuGet-packages promise intact.
      The same FrameworkReference is what lets the G5 lane 3a-1 arrivals below use
      IMemoryCache, ILogger, IOptions and IHostEnvironment with no extra package.
    -->
    <FrameworkReference Include="Microsoft.AspNetCore.App" />

    <!--
      Added by G5 lane 3a-1 (nobodies-collective/Humans#866), each forced by exactly one
      arrival. Keep this list minimal — 26 .Contracts leaves reference this project and
      inherit whatever lands here.
        CsvHelper — Csv/HumansCsv.cs, the single CSV seam (memory/code/csv-use-csvhelper.md).
        Serilog   — Logging/{CurrentUserEnricher,PiiRedactionEnricher,InMemoryLogSink}.cs,
                    which implement Serilog.Core.ILogEventEnricher / ILogEventSink.
        Octokit   — Services/GitHub{Guide,CommunityKb}ContentSource.cs, the Guide and
                    community-KB markdown readers.
    -->
    <PackageReference Include="CsvHelper" />
    <PackageReference Include="Serilog" />
    <PackageReference Include="Octokit" />

    <!--
      Added by G5 lane 3a-2 (nobodies-collective/Humans#866) with the AddSectionDbContext
      cluster: the generic registration seam is called from all 28 table-owning sections, so it
      has to live below every one of them, and its body names DbContext, AddDbContext,
      AddDbContextFactory, IInterceptor, CoreEventId, UseNpgsql and UseNodaTime. This is the
      moment Base stops being EF-free — approved for that reason, not by drift. It changes no
      leaf's own reference set: the compiler emits an assembly reference only for what a project
      actually uses, and no .Contracts leaf names an EF type.
        Microsoft.EntityFrameworkCore                    — DbContext, the options builders, the
                                                           interceptor base and the migration runner.
        Npgsql.EntityFrameworkCore.PostgreSQL            — UseNpgsql / NpgsqlDataSource.
        Npgsql.EntityFrameworkCore.PostgreSQL.NodaTime   — UseNodaTime on the Npgsql builder.
      Still zero ProjectReference elements — check that before adding one.
    -->
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.EntityFrameworkCore" />
    <PackageReference Include="Npgsql.EntityFrameworkCore.PostgreSQL" />
    <PackageReference Include="Npgsql.EntityFrameworkCore.PostgreSQL.NodaTime" />
  </ItemGroup>

</Project>
